35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found out that setting up desks upstairs takes a few minutes every single morning! Also, some of us get here way earlier than others. We have to be careful about that!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are more rigid than I expected. We are paying for empty space, and every change to the layout incurs a specific fee. We must be precise with our plan to avoid wasting the budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a conflict between the layout and our needs. The survey shows a strong desire for daylight, yet the current plan leaves several people without it. We must address this disparity openly.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The data is quite telling. There is a significant noise disparity between the corridor and the windows, and the physical setup of our workstations requires a tedious, long-term adjustment process. We cannot ignore these environmental stressors.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"It's a bit scary that every little change costs money, isn't it? But knowing that now means we can be really thoughtful about where we sit so we don't have to move again!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"If we have to spend time plugging things in every day, that's time we aren't playing or working! We should pick a layout where we don't have to waste those minutes every morning.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Exactly. Since the budget is limited and the billing is based on area, we cannot afford trial and error. We need a layout that is final and efficient from the start.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Efficiency is important, but we must be honest about the trade-offs. If some desks lack light while others have it, we need to decide how to allocate those spots fairly rather than leaving it to chance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Fairness is a vague concept. The real issue is that a poorly positioned desk is a permanent drain on productivity. If we ignore the noise levels and the time it takes to calibrate a workstation, we're failing.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"I totally agree that we should be careful! But let's not forget that being near our friends makes us more productive too! If we plan it right now, we can be happy and efficient together!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I bet we can find a way to make it fast and fun! If we don't have to scramble for seats or spend forever plugging in, we'll have more energy for the day!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Energy is irrelevant if the budget is depleted by poor planning. We must prioritize a layout that minimizes the need for future adjustments and optimizes the space we are already paying for.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we prioritize only the budget and the physical environment, we risk ignoring the human friction that arises from inequality. We need a system for who gets the window seats, or resentment will grow.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Resentment is a byproduct of inefficiency. If we simply place people where the noise is lowest and the ergonomics are stable, the ""human friction"" vanishes. Logic dictates that comfort is the only sustainable foundation for any layout.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I think we can do both! If we pick a layout that's comfortable and fits the budget, we can also make sure we're sitting next to people we get along with. That way, everyone stays happy!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm thinking we should definitely avoid anything that makes us waste time in the morning! Let's make sure our new seats are ready to go so we can start our day with a big smile!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,We have the facts now. We are paying for space we don't use and paying for every single move. Let's ensure the option we choose is the most cost-effective and permanent one.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I hope we can all agree that a ""permanent"" solution requires more than just a budget. We must explicitly decide how to handle the window seats so no one feels overlooked or unfairly treated.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,It is amusing how you all focus on budgets and feelings. The only objective truth is that noise and physical strain are constant. We must prioritize the window side to ensure a sustainable environment.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree that the window side is great, but let's make sure we're all happy with who we're sitting next to! If we're thoughtful now, we'll save money and stay best friends!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
