60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option A sounds like a race, but I found out that takes way too much time every morning! I don't want to waste my gaps plugging in cables. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is a financial disaster given the daily setup time and potential for chaos. Option B is even worse, as it guarantees recurring costs for every shift. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option C creates a permanent hierarchy of light and noise. If we choose it, we must explicitly agree on who takes the less desirable seats to avoid future resentment. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A and B are illogical. Constant movement destroys the ergonomic calibration I've identified as essential and exposes us to fluctuating noise levels. Stability is the only rational choice. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option C is perfect! It means we can decide exactly where we sit and stay close to each other without spending more money later. I'm so happy we agree! I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone likes Option C! It's the best because we can just sit down and start our day without any boring setup time. I'm so glad we're all on the same page!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"It is the only logical conclusion. By fixing the positions, we eliminate recurring facility fees and stop the waste of our limited budget. This is the most sustainable path forward for the team.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Since we have reached a consensus on Option C, let's not leave the actual seat assignments to chance. We need to discuss the window and noise disparities now so the allocation is transparent and fair.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Transparency is a fine goal, but let's be realistic. The window side is objectively superior for focus. I expect the allocation to reflect a logical prioritization of productivity over mere sentiment.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"Let's just make sure we all feel good about it! If we're all kind and thoughtful about where we sit, I know we can find a way that makes everyone smile!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm just so happy we're not doing the race-to-the-desk thing! Now we can spend all that extra time together and have the most wonderful, cozy office ever! This is going to be great!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"The decision is made. As long as we finalize the map now and avoid any further changes, we can keep the costs under control and maintain the budget. Let us conclude this.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree the decision is made, but let's be honest: some seats are worse than others. We should decide now who takes the interior wall so no one feels they were pushed there by habit.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"The interior wall is a liability. Since we've agreed on fixed desks, the only logical step is to assign the window side to those who actually value a focused, low-noise environment. Let's not overcomplicate a simple optimization.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I think we can all be happy if we just talk it out! Let's pick our neighbors and our spots together so everyone feels loved and included. I'm so glad we're doing this!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so excited! Let's make the map together and make sure it's super cozy! I can't wait to have my own special spot where I can just jump right in!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over!""}]}"
